prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and September to October came in under 90% of normal in 37 of 75 years, more than any other pair. In 2026 so far, March to April on the middle of the grids came in at 37% of normal. Grid 18508 shows a preliminary estimate of 44.8 for August to September 2026, and that is an estimate from NOAA rain, not RMA&rsquo;s index. Grid 18808 had its driest year in 2007 at 66%.</p>"}
